  "conclusion_boundaries": [
    "The V and S estimands are algebraically coupled; they are different questions with separate original nulls, NOT statistically independent/ecologically orthogonal replicates.",
    "Positive native V and missing or negative native S can arise from unequal group-average overlap slack; these source means do not identify cause, avoidance, true occupancy, or resource competition.",
    "Pairwise epsilon is nonnegative because min(aq,bv) >= min(a,b)*min(q,v); epsilon=0 if paired horizontal cell masses are equal in every supported cell, but may also be zero in other special cases.",
    "Native panel V-S equals the difference between original other and same mean epsilon exactly, under original common averaging weights. Original native 4/4 have other mean epsilon > same mean epsilon.",
    "Terrain panel V_rel-S_rel can be derived from summaries, but individual self/other epsilon components are not carried in the preserved terrain summary; do not fabricate their values.",
    "No separate permutation test was run for epsilon or its group contrast, and no statement about statistical strength of the gap follows from this deterministic decomposition.",
    "Source relative-height bins and smoothed 0.5 prior affect overlap values; source original tests remain unchanged.",
    "Four eligible study-year panels are only two bat species; no physical vertical-gap or external mechanism is demonstrated."
